WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.319 --> 00:00:07.429
Artificial intelligence researchers at
DeepMind have mastered Pong, Chess, and Go

00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:10.740
but some games are on another level.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.320
The game of StarCraft II one of the most

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.630
complicated video games ever created. It
is a real-time strategy game which means

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:23.200
that you don't take turns you play and
you have to play fast.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.900
It was clear that StarCraft would be a great grand
challenge for us to tackle using an

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.559
artificial intelligence, the techniques
we love namely neural networks, deep

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:45.680
reinforcement learning and so on so
forth.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.149
My name is Oriol Vinyals and I'm the

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:50.880
lead researcher of the AlphaStar
project.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.580
AlphaStar is an artificial intelligence system that plays the game StarCraft II.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.899
So the first element of

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:01.410
StarCraft that's quite different is that
you don't get to see what's happening on

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.100
the other side of the board that is
what we call imperfect information and

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:10.140
is a key challenge that neither in Chess
or Go are present. Another key

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.830
difference is that the pieces of Chess
or what we call units in StarCraft are

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:20.549
created throughout the game, right, so you
start with very very few units and what

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:26.250
you're doing is deciding which pieces
are you gonna invest in creating next.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.689
And that's very important because at the
same time you must counter pieces or

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:34.430
units that the other player is thinking
about without having perfect information.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:39.810
The first step of AlphaStar is can you
predict where a human is gonna click

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.740
what's the most likely move so
essentially AlphaStar is gathering

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.759
information from the game where all its
units are it's getting all this data

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:53.250
into, not a program, but rather a
mathematical entity that is called

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.860
neural network that is able to then
process all this information.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.680
We never hard coded what this processing means
this was fully learned from, first

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.520
imitation learning, trying to imitate
human moves and later on self play

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.929
through the AlphaStar League and after
this processing many layers of

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:14.460
computation of learned behavior at the top
there is essentially a single action

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.180
that will be sent back to the game, and
so this action could be create a new

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.230
unit create a worker, send this worker
to scout, move the camera to this

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.700
location and that's essentially what AlphaStar is.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.300
Every basically 20 milliseconds in the game and every
action you see here is a result of

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.180
computation using this neural network.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:41.460
By January 2019 AlphaStar was able to beat two professional players under special test conditions.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.780
But people wanted to see if it could reach the GrandMaster level.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.260
Beating the best players at the full game.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.040
What's quite critical is that
humans are very creative at playing this

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.390
game so once we went online with this
agent we faced all sorts of creative

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:02.460
strategies that we could not possibly
have ourselves designed. So the very

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:05.430
first game that we entered we were
playing against obviously someone we

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.410
don't know, so it really was like a lot
of adrenaline and a great moment to let

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.980
people essentially experience what it is
to play against such a strong AI.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.620
AlphaStar progressed by playing against
itself, against a range of human players

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.580
and crucially by playing against other
AI agents.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.800
We have this league of agents

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:30.480
where all the agents are doing self play
in a manner that is perhaps a bit more

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.640
advanced than what has been done before
and there we did perhaps the most

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:40.560
research advances in the last few months
in which we discovered that it's not

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.360
sufficient to have only one agent that
its sole purpose is to beat itself and

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:50.580
its past versions of itself. It's very
important to add agents that find flaws

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:56.100
in the main agents right, so we call
these agents exploiter agents and if you

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.269
will it's kind of asking for a friend to
beat your current strategy and maybe

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:04.050
this strategy that is going to beat you
is not a great strategy in isolation but

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:08.430
it's certainly gonna help you become a
better player and that core idea plus

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:13.200
then some extra developments in
imitation learning and reinforcement

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.790
learning that we had in the project
created an artificial intelligence agent

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:23.780
that can play the game of StarCraft II at
a GrandMaster level.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:29.460
Actually I used to play the game back
the 90s I played quite seriously the

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.080
first version of the game one of the sad
things that happened is that I kind of

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.960
waited too long to play against AlphaStar.
So the team was really like

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.270
Oriol you should play, at some point I
decided okay I'll play against the agent

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:47.490
I played when it was just strong enough
that there was no chance for me to win

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:53.780
and I just basically lost the window for
me to kind of defeat the agent sadly so

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.240
cool, victory not for me

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.729
AlphaStar has broken into the top 200

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:02.909
players in Europe at StarCraft II
playing the full version of the game

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:04.880
with all three alien races.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.750
We are here not trying to solve

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.949
StarCraft we're trying to utilize
StarCraft for the purpose of advancing

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:16.500
AI research but be applied to any domain
that utilizes artificial intelligence in

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.389
any of its components and enhance for
instance its robustness its capabilities

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:25.650
to do imitation learning from experts
and other things that we deem super

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:30.300
important and that StarCraft really lets
us test on one of the most complicated

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.580
video games ever created.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.650
Success in the real world is a little more complicated

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:41.069
computer games can readily provide the
data points an AI needs to master a

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:46.349
challenge but not every problem provides
so much accurate feedback.

00:05:46.349 --> 00:05:53.000
The integration of AI into everyday life
will be a much longer battle

